## 🔒 Security Best Practices

| Practice | Why it's Important |
|----------|-------------------|
| ✅ Encrypt at rest | Data protection against stolen storage |
| ✅ Rotate secrets regularly | Limit impact of credential leaks |
| ✅ Audit secret access | Know who accessed what and when |
| ✅ Least privilege | Services only get secrets they need |
| ✅ Destroy secrets after use | Don't cache in memory longer than needed |
| ✅ Version control secrets (understood) | Audit secrets changes |
| ❌ Version control real secrets | Exposes all credentials! |
| ❌ Use default secrets | Make it easier for attackers |

---

## 🔄 Secret Rotation Best Practices

### AWS Secrets Manager - Automatic Rotation
```javascript
// Configure rotation in AWS Console or Terraform
module "aws_secretsmanager_secret_rotation" {
  provider = aws.us-east-1

  secret_arn               = aws_secretsmanager_secret.my.secret_arn
  depends_on               = [aws_secretsmanager_secret.my]
  rotate_after_immediately = true

  rules {
    automatically_after_days = 30  # Rotate every 30 days
    service_linked_role_arn  = aws_iam_role.secrets_manager_rotation.arn
  }
}
```

### Manual Rotation
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

// Generate new secret
function generateSecureSecret(length = 32) {
  return crypto.randomBytes(length).toString('base64');
}

// Rotate secret flow
async function rotateSecret(oldSecret) {
  const newSecret = generateSecureSecret(64);

  // 1. Store in vault/secrets manager
  await storeSecret('new-secret', newSecret);

  // 2. Graceful transition period (0-15 minutes)
  await allowTransitionTime();

  // 3. Update application
  const appId = 'my-app';
  await updateAppConfig(appId, newSecret);

  // 4. Clean up old secret
  await deleteSecret('old-secret');

  // 5. Log rotation event
  await auditLog({ action: 'ROTATE', oldSecret, newSecret });

  return newSecret;
}
```

